      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CLASSIC ROYALE (4) is the one to beat with one win and three placings from five starts here, benefiting from the inside draw to bounce back. His eighth at Northam CL1 was only just over three lengths off in provincial company, and his second at this venue two starts back was impressive after being held up near the 250m. INVINCIBLE RUBY (3) adds strength after a first-up fourth in a Belmont Park CL3, closing well behind Harbour Rise, and faces an easier task second-up. The 60.5kg weighs her down, but her two wins and six placings at 1100m keep her competitive. CASINO ROYALE (1) is in form, having won a BM56+ at Leinster and placing third at Leonora, plus the 3kg claim helps offset the higher weight despite the wide barrier. I'M EUGENE (6) is a place chance, second-up with proven 1100m experience, reuniting with Jordan Turner after a sixth-place finish where he lacked a finishing kick. WHAT HAVE YOU DONE (5) is next best.",
